->actually, to identify gems, 'e'ngrave with them. If it is a worthless
->piece of glass, it will say "you write in the dust with a [color] gem"
->If it is a gemstone, it will say "you engrave in the rock with a [color] gem"

Note that this isn't *quite* true.  Although all worthless pieces of glass
merely write in the dust, there are also some gemstones which do this.
(I believe that jade and fluorite are among them.)  So, in other words,
if it engraves, it's valuable.  But if it doesn't, there's nothing more
that you can tell from using that method.
